.Dd October 4, 2026
.Dt XLOCK-INVOKE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xlock-invoke
.Nd run xlock as Lock Screen or Lock Desktop
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm Cm xlock-screen
.Op Ar xlock-args
.Nm Cm xlock-desktop
.Op Ar xlock-args
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs
.Xr xlock-run 1
with one window-manager class and the flags that class needs.
The two classes must not share flags.
.Cm xlock-screen
is opaque.
It passes
.Fl hide ,
.Fl background Cm black ,
and
.Fl mode Cm random
to
.Xr xlock 1 .
.Xr xlock-run 1
keeps a black underlay behind that class for the whole lock.
.Pp
.Cm xlock-desktop
is sheer when
.Xr picom 1
is running.
It passes
.Cm +hide
and
.Fl mode Cm random ,
so the saver can show the session through it.
When picom is not running, the same opaque path as
.Cm xlock-screen
is used, including that class name.
.Pp
.Ar xlock-args
are appended after those flags.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "XLOCK_RUN"
.It Ev DISPLAY
X server.
The default is
.Pa :0 .
.It Ev XLOCK
.Xr xlock 1
binary.
The default is
.Nm xlock
in
.Ev PATH .
.It Ev XLOCK_RUN
.Xr xlock-run 1
binary.
The default is
.Nm xlock-run
in
.Ev PATH .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 1 when
.Nm xlock-run
is not found.
A missing or unknown class exits 2.
Otherwise the exit status is that of
.Xr xlock-run 1 .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr picom 1 ,
.Xr xlock 1 ,
.Xr xlock-run 1 ,
.Xr xlock-screen 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Devin Teske Aq Mt dteske@FreeBSD.org
